 This document describes known limitations of the Entire CLI.

+## Agent Hooks
+
+### macOS Launch Checks Can Stall Hook Startup
+
+On macOS, a wedged Gatekeeper/code-signing service can prevent the `entire`
+binary from reaching Go startup. The diagnostic signature is that even
+`entire --version` hangs, and process samples show the binary stuck in
+`_dyld_start`.
+
+When this happens, hook parsing and internal Go timeouts cannot run because
+`main()` has not started yet. The Claude Code `SessionStart` production hook
+wrapper therefore runs `entire hooks claude-code session-start` as a child with
+a short timeout. If the child does not finish in time, the wrapper emits a valid
+Claude JSON `systemMessage` and exits successfully so Claude Code startup is not
+blocked.
+
+If `entire --version` also hangs outside Claude Code, restart the wedged macOS
+launch-check service. In reported cases, killing the stuck `syspolicyd` process
+allowed the binary to launch again.
+
